pending on their fatty acid composition</article-title><source>Clin Nutr</source><year>2005</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>822</fpage><lpage>829</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15978704</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.clnu.2005.05.003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rothe</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Oser</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Valet</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dihydrorhodamine 123: a new flow cytometric indicator for respiratory burst activity in neutrophil granulocytes</article-title><source>Naturwissenschaften</source><year>1988</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>354</fpage><lpage>355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3211206</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00368326</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emmend&#x000f6;rffer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hecht</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lohmann-Matthes</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Roesler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A fast and easy method to determine the production of reactive oxygen intermediates by human and murine phagocytes using dihydrorhodamine 123</article-title><source>J Immunol Methods</source><year>1990</year><volume>131</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>275</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2391431</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-1759(90)90198-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirt</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Nebe</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Birr</surname><given-names>C</given-na